    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen the completion item list is empty, I get the error in the title and native LSP config.  So far I've only tested this with Intelephense.\n\nI use rocks.nvim for plugin management atm:\n\n```toml\n[plugins.\"mini.nvim\"]\ngit = \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\"\nrev = \"6be765891c95242f6b8ebd3a25aa285ab3e9f6de\"\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe error to not occur and pollute/interfere with trying to code\n\n## Notes\n\nI didn't have this issue with mini.nvim 0.15 but I am using the new mini.snippets LSP server as well.  I'm not sure if that plays a role in this.\n\nRelevant to this LSP, I have a `.nvim/snippets/global.json` but that just is `{}` as I got focused onto other things.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI don't know if this is specific to Intelephense or how I have the LSP configured.  However, I have not noticed a pattern of consistency to reproduce.  Whether I choose an item, finish typing it out, force-close the popup, etc... it just happens when it wants to it feels, but it's pretty frequent.\n\nSo I feel that may be a good/better starting point:\n\n```lua\n-- lsp/intelephense.lua\nreturn {\n    cmd = { \"intelephense\", \"--stdio\" },\n    root_markers = { \"composer.json\", \".git\" },\n    filetypes = { \"php\" },\n    capabilities = {\n        textDocument = {\n            completion = {\n                completionItem = {\n                    snippetSupport = false,\n                },\n            },\n        },\n    },\n    settings = {\n        intelephense = {\n            diagnostics = {\n                enable = false,\n            },\n        },\n    },\n}\n```",
